# Scenario diag-stic2-idle-pass (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05, D-10): outcome pass, exit 0. The program ivs-diag-stic-2 through the
# project boot stub contract 2 with the zero graphics ROM and no input line, so the selector read at 01FE returns the low byte FF
# and the program stays at scene 0 for the whole run. This is the idle control of the six diag-stic2 scenarios (D-04): the
# picture is the literal F-M0 (the cards only: color 1 everywhere except the 25 set pixels of card 2 in cell (6, 10), color 2),
# which proves the program, not the core, adds no moving object, no strip and no delay. The asserts are the hand-derived
# expectations of data/golden/diag-stic2-idle-pass.expect (derivation in docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md, section (f),
# written before the program): the same lines in the same order as the committed idle block of that document, and the same as
# the .expect (golden-expect-drift). It differs from diag-stic2-mob-pass and diag-stic2-border-pass in the video and input
# digests only (data/expected/scenario-pairs.ids). It never halts.
ivss 1
id diag-stic2-idle-pass
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-2.ivsc
capture video 0 10
run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 00FF
assert mem 02F3 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 1 displayed == yes
assert frame 9 displayed == yes
assert frame 5 hash == 17df47dfad24a8f419dff876ce3f1d970dd1f0e914b1e8ce3638fbc9904ab39c
assert frame 1 pixel 80 48 == 2
assert frame 9 pixel 84 52 == 2
assert frame 9 pixel 85 52 == 1
assert frame 9 pixel 0 0 == 1
assert frame 9 pixel 158 95 == 1
assert video count == 10
